> Plot Example

A simple plotting example: noisy samples of the Doppler function, the true mean, and a B-spline fit -- the same program in C++ and in each language binding: C#, D, Go, Guile, Java, JavaScript, Lua, OCaml, Octave, Perl, PHP, Python, R, Ruby and Tcl.

Each block runs in the nix shell `.#report-<language>`, which provides the language and its nix-built datamunge binding, so nothing needs building first (the first run of a language builds its binding, later runs reuse it). Each program saves its figure under `build/`, and the block shows it.

\tabs(
\tab(C++,
```{cpp, nix-shell="git+file:../..#report-cpp", cmd="c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && {bin}", file="figures/plot.svg"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  dm::set_seed(42);
  const auto doppler = [](const dm::Vector<>& x) { return dm::sin(20 / (x + 0.25)); };
  const auto x = dm::runif(0, 1, 1000);
  const auto y = doppler(x) + dm::rnorm(0, 1, 1000);
  const auto xseq = dm::seql(0, 1, 1000);
  const auto yseq = doppler(xseq);
  const dm::BSR bsr(x, y, 100);
  const auto yfit = bsr.predict(xseq);
  const auto plt = dm::plot()
    .title("Doppler data")
    .points(x, y, "Samples", "#edc78799")
    .lines(xseq, yseq, "True Mean", "#c80a2c", 3.)
    .lines(xseq, yfit, "Estimated Mean", "#2c0ac8", 3.)
    .x_label("X").y_label("doppler(X)")
    .size(1000, 600);
  dm::mkdir("build");
  plt.save("build/plot.svg");
}
```
// result_begin:
// \image(figures/plot.svg)
// result_end
)
\tab(Python,
```{python, nix-shell="git+file:../..#report-python", file="figures/plot_python.svg"}
import os
import numpy as np
from pydatamunge import datamunge as dm

def doppler(x):
    return np.sin(20 / (np.asarray(x) + 0.25))

dm.set_seed(42)
x = np.array(dm.runif(0, 1, 1000))
y = doppler(x) + np.array(dm.rnorm(0, 1, 1000))
xseq = np.array(dm.seql(0, 1, 1000))
yseq = doppler(xseq)
yfit = dm.BSplineRegression(x, y, 100).predict(xseq)
os.makedirs("build", exist_ok=True)
(dm.RPlot.create()
    .title("Doppler data")
    .points(x, y, "Samples", dm.RGB(237, 199, 135, 0.6), 4.0)
    .lines(xseq, yseq, "True Mean", dm.RGB(200, 10, 44), 3.0)
    .lines(xseq, yfit, "Estimated Mean", dm.RGB(44, 10, 200), 3.0)
    .xlab("X")
    .ylab("doppler(X)")
    .save("build/plot_python.svg"))
```
